*
* MVPKGOS(OP, P1, P2, RESULT) — the one call the portable MVPKG client makes
* for operations that are not pure MultiValue.  This is the Rocket UniData
* port; it matches the MVX MVPKGOS (MKDIR / UNTAR) and adds the two ops that
* let the package manager maintain UniData's shared CallC library:
*
*   OP = "MKDIR"    P1 = path                 -> create P1 (and parents)
*   OP = "UNTAR"    P1 = tarball  P2 = destdir -> extract P1 into P2
*   OP = "CALLC"    P1 = pkgdir   P2 = name    -> stage the package's native
*                     CallC contribution (P1/udt-callc) and rebuild the
*                     shared libu2callc.so from every contribution installed;
*                     a package without a udt-callc/ is a silent no-op
*   OP = "REBUILD"                             -> rebuild the shared library
*                     from the currently-staged contributions (no install)
*   OP = "PLATFORM"                            -> RESULT = "<system>:<arch>:<end>",
*                     the identity the client sends the registry so it serves
*                     the matching prebuilt binary (else source).  UniData is
*                     system "udt"; arch is the host machine (uname -m); end is
*                     "le"/"be" (endianness — the axis for BASIC objects and
*                     data files, as arch is for native code).
*
* UniData loads exactly one libu2callc.so, so native add-ons cannot each own
* it — they are aggregated.  The heavy lifting (compile, merge cfuncdef,
* gencdef/genefs/genfunc, relink, install) lives in the udt-callc-build
* helper, installed at $UDTHOME/bin/udt-callc-build by the mv_package
* UniData setup; MVPKGOS just drives it.  RESULT is "" on success or an
* error message.  These shell out through EXECUTE "!...", so the caller
* needs the unrestricted privilege tier — installing software is privileged.
   SUBROUTINE MVPKGOS(OP, P1, P2, RESULT)
   RESULT = ""
   OP = OCONV(OP, "MCU")
   UDT = GETENV("UDTHOME")
   BUILDER = UDT : "/bin/udt-callc-build"
   BEGIN CASE
      CASE OP = "MKDIR"
         EXECUTE '!mkdir -p "':P1:'"'
      CASE OP = "UNTAR"
         EXECUTE '!mkdir -p "':P2:'" && tar -xzf "':P1:'" -C "':P2:'"'
      CASE OP = "CALLC"
         EXECUTE '!"':BUILDER:'" add "':P1:'" "':P2:'"'
      CASE OP = "REBUILD"
         EXECUTE '!"':BUILDER:'"'
      CASE OP = "PLATFORM"
         * "!" shell escapes don't feed CAPTURING here, so route the probes
         * through a temp file and read them back.  arch = uname -m; endian
         * from a two-byte dump (0201 = little, 0102 = big) — the axis for
         * compiled BASIC objects + data files.  RESULT = "<sys>:<arch>:<end>".
         TMPF = "/tmp/mvpkg_plat_" : @USERNO
         EXECUTE '!uname -m > "':TMPF:'" 2>/dev/null'
         OSREAD ARCH FROM TMPF ELSE ARCH = ""
         ARCH = TRIM(CONVERT(CHAR(10):CHAR(13), "  ", ARCH))
         IF ARCH = "" THEN ARCH = "unknown"
         EXECUTE "!printf '\1\2' | od -An -tx2 | tr -d ' ' > " : TMPF : " 2>/dev/null"
         OSREAD EW FROM TMPF ELSE EW = ""
         EXECUTE '!rm -f "':TMPF:'"'
         IF EW[1,4] = "0102" THEN ENDIAN = "be" ELSE ENDIAN = "le"
         RESULT = "udt:" : ARCH : ":" : ENDIAN
      CASE 1
         RESULT = "MVPKGOS: unknown op ":OP
   END CASE
   RETURN
